## SUBGROUP/INTERACTION EXTRACTION (USING EXISTING LABELS ONLY)

If this paper reports subgroup analyses or treatment × moderator interactions:
- Use INTERACTION_TERM for the interaction coefficient
- Use SE for the interaction standard error
- Use P_VALUE for the interaction p-value
- Use SUBGROUP_EFFECT for within-subgroup effect sizes
- Use SAMPLE_SIZE_ARM for subgroup sample sizes
- Encode subgroup variable and value in the "context" field

Example: "Age × treatment interaction: beta=0.15, SE=0.08, p=0.06; effect in older adults: d=0.52 (n=84)"
→ 5 spans with same grouping_id:
  - INTERACTION_TERM: 0.15, context: "age × treatment interaction beta"
  - SE: 0.08, context: "SE of age × treatment interaction"
  - P_VALUE: 0.06, context: "p-value for age × treatment interaction"
  - SUBGROUP_EFFECT: 0.52, context: "effect in older adults (age >65)"
  - SAMPLE_SIZE_ARM: 84, context: "n for older adults subgroup"

## CRITICAL REMINDERS
- ANCHOR TOKENS ARE REQUIRED for effect/beta/ratio/test-stat labels
- Years (1900-2100) and naked integers are NOT effect sizes
- Character offsets refer to FULL_TEXT, char_end is exclusive
- Always extract BOTH bounds of a confidence interval as separate spans
- Group related statistics with the SAME grouping_id
- Sort output by char_start, then char_end
- No duplicate spans
- If unsure and no anchor token → prefer SAMPLE_SIZE, MEAN, SD, or omit

Return ONLY the JSON object, no additional text.